message: "If you use these figures or data, please cite them as below, and cite the primary sources listed in docs/REFERENCES.md for any individual value."
title: "The Allowed Universe: real objects plotted between the hard limits of physics"
type: dataset
authors:
  - alias: QuantumNovice
repository-code: "https://github.com/QuantumNovice/awesome-universal-limits"
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-03
keywords:
  - physics
  - physical-limits
  - scale-comparison
  - data-visualization
  - log-log
  - astrophysics
  - open-data
  - science-communication
abstract: >-
  Log-log charts that place real objects, from a hydrogen molecule to the Milky Way,
  inside the bounds physics allows: spin, oscillation, speed, acceleration, mass,
  density, pressure, temperature and lifetime against size; energy per kilogram and
  power; charge, voltage, magnetic fields, radio links and light; black hole spins and
  pulsars; chemical binding, material strength, sound, flow and volumes; organism sizes,
  genomes and epidemic spread; buildings; AI model size, compute and benchmarks; human
  cognition, research output and the scale of numbers. Every value carries a primary
  source; limit lines are computed from formulas using CODATA 2022 constants. An
  interactive Vue site draws the same data with hover tooltips.
